{
  "_how_to": [
    "This file says which column (or JSON field) in each provider's file gives TRUST each piece of information it needs. You edit it; nobody needs to change code.",
    "To change a name: find the feed (e.g. \"hr\") and the field (e.g. \"SAM_ACCOUNT\"), put the column name exactly as it appears in the provider's file FIRST in the list, save, and upload the file again.",
    "Case, spaces, underscores and dashes don't matter anywhere, here or in the files: \"Email - Work\", \"email_work\" and \"EMAIL WORK\" are the same. Close spellings are matched anyway and shown on the upload result.",
    "A name starting with * means \"the column name ends with this\": \"*SAM_Acct\" finds \"Worker_SAM_Acct\". If two columns end that way, neither is used and the upload result says so.",
    "The names on the left (\"SAM_ACCOUNT\", \"Worker\", ...) are TRUST's own; don't change them. Only the lists on the right are yours.",
    "If a field isn't in the file, the file still loads; only the metrics that need it show No data.",
    "Keep it valid JSON: names in double quotes, separated by commas. A trailing comma is fine. Keys starting with _ are notes and are ignored.",
    "Feeds with no fields have no layout yet: add the real column names when the file arrives."
  ],
